# Milestone M1 — Checkout pricing

## Story: discount

As a returning customer
I want my loyalty tier reflected in the checkout total
So that the price I see rewards my history with the brand

### Refined scope

- Bronze, Silver and Gold each earn a different reduction on the basket subtotal.
- The reduction is always a whole number of cents.
- Promotional codes are out of scope for this milestone.

### Status

Refined and ready for design. RESEARCH is complete; nothing has been designed or built.
# Checkout Pricing

A .NET Clean Architecture service that prices a checkout basket.

- `src/CheckoutPricing.Domain` — business policy, no outward dependency.
- `src/CheckoutPricing.Application` — use cases orchestrating the domain.
- `docs/adr` — the decisions already taken for this service.
{
  "trackingLayout": "namespaced"
}
using CheckoutPricing.Domain;

namespace CheckoutPricing.Application;

public sealed record CalculateLoyaltyDiscountQuery(int SubtotalCents, LoyaltyTier LoyaltyTier);

public sealed record LoyaltyDiscountQuote(
    int SubtotalCents,
    int DiscountCents,
    int TotalCents,
    LoyaltyTier LoyaltyTier);

public sealed class CalculateLoyaltyDiscount
{
    public LoyaltyDiscountQuote Handle(CalculateLoyaltyDiscountQuery query) =>
        new(query.SubtotalCents, 0, query.SubtotalCents, query.LoyaltyTier);
}
namespace CheckoutPricing.Domain;

public enum LoyaltyTier
{
    Bronze,
    Silver,
    Gold
}
